This is the JSON for a folder in the dataroom. It is used to define the folder and the documents that should be published to the dataroom.

The folder_id is the ID of the folder in the dataroom.
The auto_publish_immediately is a boolean that indicates if the documents should be published immediately.
The auto_publish_scheduled_time is a string that indicates the time at which the documents should be published.
The created_at is the date and time the folder was created.
The dataroom_id is the ID of the dataroom.
The description is a string that describes the folder.
The label is a string that is the name of the folder.
The linked_item_id is the ID of the item that the folder is linked to.
The linked_item_label is a string that is the name of the item that the folder is linked to.

So this becomes a query:

Return all documents that have the [ correspondent ] equal to [ Aegis Aged Care Group ]

"linked_item_id": "7",
"linked_item_label": "Aegis Aged Care Group",
"linked_item_type": "correspondent",

And as the publish rule is set to "immediately", any documents that match this query should be returned in the dataroom query.


The published metadata fields published_metadata_fields specify which metadata fields should be published to the dataroom.

So in this example, the published metadata fields are:

"title",
"content",
"created",
"correspondent",
"document_type",
"archive_serial_number",
"original_md5",
"tags",
"original_file_size"

And the published custom field ids published_custom_field_ids specify which custom fields should be published to the dataroom.

